; Leaf library: no library dependencies at all.
;
; `Cow_table` is the copy-on-write sharded map that most of the engine's read-mostly
; caches are built on. `Id_table` is its integer-keyed counterpart, used where the key is
; a venue-assigned id (IBKR order ids and req ids) and is therefore already an index.
; Both live here, rather than in `concurrency`, because two lower-level libraries need them
; and both sit *below* `concurrency` in the dependency graph — `logging` (which everything,
; including `concurrency`, depends on) and `latency_profiling`. Putting them in
; `concurrency` would have made their use of it a dependency cycle, and duplicating the
; implementations in each would leave several copies of the trickiest code in the repo.
;
; Keep this library dependency-free. It is the bottom of the graph.
(library
 (name ds)
 (public_name dio.data_structures)
 ; the wrapped alias module is `Ds`, so call sites read `Ds.Cow_table` / `Ds.Id_table`
 (modules Cow_table Id_table))
